storywiki && git remote set-url origin $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git && git pull -q && git log --oneline | head -2; git diff 55ae7df HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1500"]], "output": "```console\nd293a4c Outline rev 9: Brief rev 4 (GREG lineage, deciding contrast, small-n fall-back)\n55ae7df Tidy the outline header\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n-| C2 | **Bias–variance:** model-based predictors show signed bias that grows away from the source range (compression toward the source mean); the difference estimator removes it and costs a stated amount of variance — or it does not | Signed error vs true score per method class, extrapolation split especially; bias and variance computed **per target over subset draws first (≥100 draws where cheap), then summarised across targets**, with the Monte Carlo SE of each per-target bias shown (no pooling of targets and draws into one \"variance\"); λ, ε tuned on sources only **with a tuning split that mimics the evaluation split** (§3); sensitivity of the primary endpoint to λ and ε; LOO-vs-naive fit bias for sampled items | Fig. 3 (signed error vs true target score), Table 3 (bias² / variance / RMSE by method) |\n-| C3 | **Factorial ablation:** a win is attributable to design, estimator, or their combination, not to a weak comparator | design {uniform, stratified, uncertainty-PPS, balanced, anchor medoids, IRT-CAT} × estimator {mean/Hájek, calibrated regression, model-based, difference}; analysis lists the **meaningful cells** (e.g. anchor medoids × difference needs weights), costs the grid, and if needed runs the full grid at the primary n only and a reduced grid across n. IRT-CAT is a **different protocol** (per-target items; paired with uniform by target at the same n and the same number of starting-item draws) and its cells are marked as such | Fig. 4 (heatmap, RMSE ratio, primary n; one panel per split or interp+extrap) |\n+| C2 | **Bias–variance:** model-based predictors show signed bias that grows away from the source range (compression toward the source mean); the difference estimator removes it and costs a stated amount of variance — or it does not | Signed error vs true score per method class, extrapolation split especially; bias and variance computed **per target over subset draws first (≥100 draws where cheap), then summarised across targets**, with the Monte Carlo SE of each per-target bias shown (no pooling of targets and draws into one \"variance\"); λ, ε tuned on sources only **with a tuning split that mimics the evaluation split** (§3); sensitivity of the primary endpoint to λ and ε; LOO-vs-naive fit bias for sampled items; for the target-recalibrated estimator (§3b): fall-back rate to the Hájek mean by n and split reported beside the error (results at n where it exceeds 20% marked as mostly the fall-back) | Fig. 3 (signed error vs true target score), Table 3 (bias² / variance / RMSE by method) |\n+| C3 | **Factorial ablation:** a win is attributable to design, estimator, or their combination, not to a weak comparator | design {uniform, stratified, uncertainty-PPS, balanced, anchor medoids, IRT-CAT} × estimator {mean/Hájek, calibrated regression, model-based, difference}; analysis lists the **meaningful cells** (e.g. anchor medoids × difference needs weights), costs the grid, and if needed runs the full grid at the primary n only and a reduced grid across n. IRT-CAT is a **different protocol** (per-target items; paired with uniform by target at the same n and the same number of starting-item draws) and its cells are marked as such. **Deciding contrast (Brief rev 4):** (stratified on source difficulty) × (target-recalibrated regression, Brief §3b) against (stratified) × (stratum-mean/Hájek) and (uniform) × (§3b); if §3b adds nothing over stratify-and-post-stratify, the paper says so and the contribution is the analysis and the robustness claim, not the estimator | Fig. 4 (heatmap, RMSE ratio, primary n; one panel per split or interp+extrap) |\n-- **HOLD (Brief rev 3):** the extrapolation paragraph below is provisional until analysis answers the Brief's §3b/§3c additions (target-recalibrated regression with a slope fitted on the target's own n answers, an optional\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "70de3d72-a35e-568b-acaa-a23d21680984", "at": 1795676724.821802, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27612, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "cab39c1a29558367e8b4fa3123da66d2", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "d7ce6540-8fd2-5469-a41f-bef64c14b2bb", "at": 1795676724.829469, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27613, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "cab39c1a29558367e8b4fa3123da66d2", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "2d87bfec-f4c6-59e2-8574-781e136ca387", "at": 1795676724.832079, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27614, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "cab39c1a29558367e8b4fa3123da66d2", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "f5741f11-64b2-5a85-a549-7c62054dda6c", "at": 1795676724.980138, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27615, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "cab39c1a29558367e8b4fa3123da66d2", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "ch